Description: Center a normal window of a fixed size, as a dialog, also without center-new-windows.
 With center-new-windows off, mutter centers only dialogs, modal dialogs and splash screens, and places a normal
 window in the first free spot, often near the top left of the monitor. A Wayland client cannot position its
 windows itself, and has no window type to tell mutter that a small window, as Claude Desktop's Quick Entry, should
 open in the middle: such a window is a normal window without a parent, and only its size is fixed, its minimum and
 maximum size being equal, which is how Electron declares a BrowserWindow which cannot be resized.
 window_place_centered() now also centers a normal window whose minimum and maximum sizes are equal. A window with
 a parent is still centered over its parent.
 .
 The stacking test fixed-size-placement checks that, with center-new-windows off, a window which can be resized is
 still placed in the first free spot, and that a window of a fixed size is centered on the monitor, from a Wayland
 and from an X11 client. The test client gains the command set_fixed_size, which sets the window's minimum and
 maximum size to its size. The reference test /wayland/toplevel/fixed-size-fullscreen of wayland-unit-tests opens a
 window of a fixed size without center-new-windows, and its first reference image shows the window in the first
 free spot, so the test moves the window there before it compares the image.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-26

diff --git a/src/core/place.c b/src/core/place.c
index 43ffd2f..c2a07bd 100644
--- a/src/core/place.c
+++ b/src/core/place.c
@@ -445,6 +445,14 @@ window_overlaps_focus_window (MetaWindow *window,
                                   &overlap);
 }
 
+/* A window whose minimum and maximum sizes are equal cannot be resized. */
+static gboolean
+window_has_fixed_size (MetaWindow *window)
+{
+  return (window->size_hints.min_width == window->size_hints.max_width &&
+          window->size_hints.min_height == window->size_hints.max_height);
+}
+
 static gboolean
 window_place_centered (MetaWindow *window)
 {
@@ -452,10 +460,17 @@ window_place_centered (MetaWindow *window)
 
   type = window->type;
 
+  /* A normal window of a fixed size is placed as a dialog is, centered,
+   * also without center-new-windows: a Wayland client cannot position its
+   * windows itself, and small windows of a fixed size which it would center,
+   * as quick entry or launcher windows, have no type which tells mutter.
+   */
   return (type == META_WINDOW_DIALOG ||
           type == META_WINDOW_MODAL_DIALOG ||
           type == META_WINDOW_SPLASHSCREEN ||
-         (type == META_WINDOW_NORMAL && meta_prefs_get_center_new_windows ()));
+         (type == META_WINDOW_NORMAL &&
+          (meta_prefs_get_center_new_windows () ||
+           window_has_fixed_size (window))));
 }
 
 static void
